Based on my multi-culture upbringing, a mixture of European and Chinese descend, in my family, expectations are centred on:
- The understanding that anyone, regardless of sex, have equal opportunities to be a certain role and take certain action, as per our abilities;
- The consideration that as being children of the universe, we all have our unique strengths and weaknesses, and we can each be intrinsically valued for those without comparisons, and more importantly to recognise that these are subject to change within the circumstances and conditions surrounding us;
- The matter that as individuals with minimal control over the condition of life, we have the responsibility to strive for the best we can be - to be compassionate towards others, to contribute to the community and the world, and to compete healthily for personal and collective values, that lead to our personal growth and the greater good of the society as a whole.

